$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure E: Cu-catalyzed sulfide
formation[4]. (2,6-Dimethylphenyl)(3,5-dimethylphenyl)sulfide S6. CuI (38
mg, 0.20 mmol) and K2CO3 (1.11 g, 8.00 mmol) were added to a metal-capped
test tube with Teflon-lined septum. The tube was evacuated and backfilled
with argon (3 cycles). 3,5-Dimethyliodobenzene (0.58 mL, 4.00 mmol),
2,6-dimethylthiophenol (0.53 mL, 4.00 mmol), 2-propanol (4.0 mL) and
ethylene glycol (0.45 mL, 8.00 mmoL) were added at room temperature and
the tube was heated to 80 °C and stirred for 24 h. The reaction mixture
was then allowed to cool to room temperature, before diluting with EtOAc
(5 mL). The reaction mixture was then filtered and concentrated in vacuo.
The crude product was purified by column chromatography on silica gel
eluting with n-hexane to yield the product (0.90 g, 93% yield) as a
yellow oil;
(3,3,4,4,5,5,6,6,7,7,8,8,9,9,10,10,10-Heptadecafluorodecyl)(3-methoxyphenyl)sulfide
S8. As described in general procedure E, 1-iodo-3-methoxybenzene (0.24
mL, 2.00 mmol),
3,3,4,4,5,5,6,6,7,7,8,8,9,9,10,10,10-heptadecafluorodecane-1-thiol (0.57
mL, 2.00 mmol), CuI (19 mg, 0.10 mmol), K2CO3 (0.56 g, 4.00 mmol),
ethylene glycol (0.23 mL, 4.00 mmol), and 2-propanol (2.0 mL), after
purification by FSPE gave
(3,3,4,4,5,5,6,6,7,7,8,8,9,9,10,10,10-heptadecafluorodecyl)(3-methoxyphenyl)sulfide
(0.96 g, 81% yield) as a yellow solid (mp 55-56 °C); mp 55-56 °C.
νmax(neat)/cm-1 2938, 2158, 1588, 1233, 1197, 115, 1031, 864, 650, 528;
δH (400 MHz, CDCl3) 2.33 - 2.50 (2H, m, S-CH2CH2), 3.09 - 3.17 (2H m,
S-CH2CH2), 3.82 (3H, s, OCH3), 6.80 (1H, ddd, J 8.2, 2.4, 0.8 Ar-H), 6.90
(1H, m, Ar-H), 6.92 - 6.97 (1H, m, Ar-H), 7.25 (1H, t, J 8.2, Ar-H); δC
(100 MHz, CDCl3) 24.5 (S-CH2CH2), 31.7 (S-CH2CH2), 55.3 (OCH3), 112.7
(Ar-CH), 115.1 (Ar-CH), 121.7 (Ar-CH), 130.1 (Ar-CH), 135.5 (Ar-C), 160.1
(Ar-C); m/z (EI) M, 586; (Found: M, 586.0247. C17H11OF17S requires, M
586.0254).
