$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of Aryl
Sulfides: To a stirred solution of iodobenzene (1.1 mmol) and
benzenethiol (1.0 mmol) in dry DMSO (2.0 mL) was added or (3.0 mol %)
followed by KOH (2.0 equiv) under nitrogen atmosphere at 135 °C for 24 h.
The progress of the reaction was monitored by TLC. After the reaction was
complete, the reaction mixture was allowed to cool, and a 1:1 mixture of
ethyl acetate/water (20 mL) was added The solvent and volatiles were
completely removed under vacuum to give the crude product, which was
purified by column chromatography (petroleum ether/ethyl acetate = 99:1)
to yield the expected product 1a (yield: In(OH)3 10% ; In2S3 15%).
(4-isopropylphenyl)(phenyl)sulfane (1c) Following the general procedure
using 4-isopropyl iodobenzene and benzenethiol provided (4-
isopropylphenyl)(phenyl)sulfane(182.50 mg) with (80% yield). Colorless
oil IR (KBr): ν 3045, 2931, 2921, 1671, 1561, 1232, 1067, 971 cm-1. 1H
NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3, TMS): δ = 7.44 - 7.11 (m, 9H), 3.03 - 2.76 (m, 1H),
1.28 (d, 6H, J = 7.0 Hz). 13C NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3, TMS): δ = 148.3,
136.8, 131.9, 131.7, 130.0, 129.0, 128.1, 127.3, 127.1, 126.4, 33.7,
23.8. Mass (ESI): m/z 251[M+Na]. Anal calcd for: C15H16S (228) C: 78.90,
H: 7.06, S: 14.04. S6 found C: 78.81, H: 6.99, S: 13.97.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Nano Indium Oxide as a Recyclable Catalyst for C-S Cross-Coupling of
Thiols with Aryl Halides under Ligand Free conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Reddy, Vutukuri Prakash; Kumar, Akkilagunta Vijay; Swapna, Kokkirala;
Rao, Kakulapati Rama
