$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for
3-chloro-4-(phenylthio)anilines. A solution of
3-bromo-4-chloro-nitrobenzene (2.0 mmol), cuprous thiophenolate (2.0
mmol), pyridine (1.0 mL), and quinoline (4.0 mL) was heated with stirring
at 220°C for 2 h. The reaction mixture was quenched with water and
extracted with EtOAc, The organic layer was sequentially washed with
brine (2 × 30 mL), dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, and concentrated in
vacuo. The crude was purified by column chromatography (SiO2,
hexane/EtOAc 80:20) to give the desired products ca 80%. Intermediate of
3-chloro-4-(phenylthio)aniline. R = Me.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient Discovery of Potent Anti-HIV Agents Targeting the Tyr181Cys
Variant of HIV Reverse Transcriptase
