$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4-(4-Nitrophenylthio)-3-phenylsydnone (8). A mixture of compound 7 (0.3
g, 0.84 mmol), p-iodonitrobenzene (0.2 g, 0.84 mmol), LiCl (0.14 g, 3.36
mmol), and Pd(PPh3)4(0.05 g, 0. 042.mmol) in 25 mL of anhydrous benzene
was refluxed for 3 h. The reaction mixture was cooled to ∼20 °C, and a
saturated solution of KF (10 mL) was added. The organic layer was
decanted, dried with potassium carbonate, and filtered through a layer of
Al2O3 (2×3 cm) with CHCl3 as the eluent. The eluate was concentrated in
vacuo, and the residue was recrystallized from a chloroform-hexane
mixture. yield: 0.21 g (80%). m.p. 115 °C. Found (%): C, 53.42; H, 2.91;
N, 13.30; S, 9.96. C14H9N3SO4. Calculated (%): C, 53.33; H, 2.88; N,
13.33; S, 10.17. 1H NMR (CDCl3), δ: 7.30, 8.15 (dd, 4 H, C6H4, AB system,
J = 12 Hz); 7.40-7.76 (m, 5 H, Ph). IR, ν/cm-1: 1764 (CO).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
