$DATUM 1,2,4,5-Tetrakis(n-hexylthio)benzene (9c). To a stirred, degassed
solution of 60% sodium hydride (w/w) in mineral oil (80 g, 2 mol) in dry
DMF (1 L), 1-hexanethiol (282 mL, 2 mol) was addded dropwisely at 0 °C.
The mixture was stirred for 30 minutes. 1,2,4,5-Tetrachlorobenzene (1)
(75.0 g, 347 mmol) was added, and the resulting mixture was heated to
gentle reflux for 24 h. After cooling to room temperature, the reaction
mixture was poured over ice (800 g). The precipitate was removed by
filtration, washed with water, and dried. Yield, 150.7 g (80%). Short
white needles. m.p.: 56-57°C. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz) δ 0.89 (m, CH3,
12H), 1.44 (m, CH2, 8H), 1.30 (m, CH2, 16H), 1.66 (m, CH2, 8H), 2.68 (t,
3J = 7.43 Hz, 3J = 7.24 Hz, CH2, 2H), 2.88 (t, 3J 7.43 Hz, 3J = 7.24 Hz,
SCH2, 6H), 7.17 (s, ArH, 2H). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 125 MHz) δ 14.0, 22.6,
28.1, 28.9, 31.4, 33.7, 129.4, 135.3 Anal. calcd. for C30H54S4: C,
66.36%; H, 10.02%; S, 23.62% Found: C, 66.25%; H, 9.83%; S, 23.99%.
