$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: S-Pentamethylphenyl Thiobenzoate (3c); Typical
Procedure: A mixture of pentamethyliodobenzene (1c; 137 mg, 0.5 mmol),
copper(I) thiobenzoate (2; 102 mg, 0.51 mmol), and HMPT (5 ml) is heated
with stirring under nitrogen at 100-110 °C for 2 h, and is then poured
into water (300 ml). The milky solution gradually separates a light brown
precipitate which is filtered off. washed with water (100 ml), sucked as
dryas possible, placed in a filter thimble, and extracted with benzene
using a Soxhlet extractor. The solvent is removed from the extract using
a rotary evaporator and the residue is trituated with hexane, which is
recrystallized from ethanol. yield: 106 mg (80%). crystalline solid. m.p.
150-152°C. Molecular Formula: C18H20OS (284.4), calc.: C 76.01, H 7.09,
found: C 76.23, H 7.14, I.R. (KBr) ν [cm-1]: 1680, 1450, 1205, 1175, 900,
770, 685, 1H-N.M.R. (CCl4/TMS, 60 MHz) δ [ppm]: 2.27 (s, 9 H); 2.38 (s, 6
H); 7.3-7.5 (m, 3 H); 7.9-8.1 (m, 2H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A convenient synthesis of S-aryl thiobenzoates from copper(I)
thiobenzoate and aryl iodides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Osuka, Atsuhiro; Ohmasa, Nobuko; Uno, Yukari; Suzuki, Hitomi
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (1983), (1), 68-9

