$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Methyl 2-[(1-methyl-4,6-dinitro-2-phenyl-1H-indol-7-yl)-thio]acetate (6).
A mixture of chloride 3 (0.33 g, 1 mmol), methyl thioglycolate (0.18 mL,
2 mmol), and Et3N (0.3 mL, 2.2 mmol) in MeOH (30 mL) was stirred at ~20°C
for 24 h. Then the solution was poured into acidified water. The
precipitate that formed was filtered off, washed with water, and dried in
air. Compound 6 (0.32 g, 80%). m.p. 127-130°C. Found (%): C, 53.64; H,
3.93; N, 10.61; S, 7.80. C18H15N3O6S. Calculated (%): C, 53.86; H, 3.77;
N, 10.47; S, 7.99. 1H NMR, δ: 3.95 (s, 3 H, Me); 4.10 (s, 2 H, CH2); 4.15
(s, 3 H, Me); 7.25 (s, 1 H, H(3)); 7.37-7.75 (m, 5 H, Ph); 9.06 (s, 1 H,
H(5)).
