$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2-(phenylthio)phenol (3a) A mixture of
thiophenol 1a (0.5 mmol, 55.0 mg), iodobenzene 2a (0.6 mmol, 122.4 mg),
CuI (10 mol %, 9.5 mg), L4 (10 mol %, 9.5 mg) and Cs2CO3 (2 equiv, 325.8
mg) in DMSO (2 mL) was stirred in N2 at 100C for 10 h. After completion
of the reaction, the mixture was quenched with saturated salt water (10
mL), the solution was extracted with ethyl acetate (3 × 10 mL). The
organic layers were combined, and dried over sodium sulfate. The pure
product was obtained by flash column chromatography on silica gel.
2-(4-bromophenylthio)-5-methylphenol (3k); Colorless liquid; Yield: 80%.
1H NMR (500 MHz, d6-DMSO): δ 9.90 (s, 1H), 7.45-7.43 (d, J= 8.3 Hz, 2H),
7.19-7.17 (d, J= 7.8 Hz, 1H), 6.99-6.97 (d, J= 8.3 Hz, 2H), 6.78 (s, 1H),
6.68-6.67 (d, J= 7.8 Hz, 1H), 2.25 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, d6-DMSO): δ
158.87, 142.18, 138.29, 136.68, 132.93, 130.08, 122.17, 119.31, 117.93,
114.57, 22.15. GC-MS (EI) [M]+: 294. HRMS (EI) calcd for C13H11BrOS [M]+:
293.9714; found 293.9723.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Facile Synthesis of 2-(Phenylthio)phenols by Copper(I)-Catalyzed Tandem
Transformation of C-S Coupling/C-H Functionalization
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
