$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Experimental Procedure for the
Synthesis of Benzothiazole. In a 15 mL two-necked flask, a mixture of
(2-iodophenylimino)triphenylphosphorane (168 mg, 0.3 mmol), thiobenzoic
acid (53 mg, 0.33 mmol), CuI (2.8 mg, 5% mol), and 1,10-phenthroline (5.2
mg, 10 mol %) in dioxane (3 mL) was stirred at room temperature under N2
atmosphere for 5 min. Then the solution was stirred at 100 &#x00B0;C for
32 h until complete consumption of starting material as monitored by TLC.
After the reaction was finished, the mixture was washed with brine,
extracted with EtOAc, dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, and evaporated under a
vacuum. The residue was purified by flash column chromatography on silica
gel (petroleum ether/ethyl acetate, 4/1) to give the product 5a.
6-Bromo-2-phenylbenzothiazole7d (5g). White solid: 62.4 mg (80% yield).
mp 150-151 &#x00B0;C&#x00B0;C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) &#x3B4; 8.13-8.07
(m, 2H), 8.06 (d, J = 1.7 Hz, 1H), 7.94 (d, J = 8.7 Hz, 1H), 7.61 (dd, J
= 8.7, 1.7 Hz, 1H), 7.56-7.48 (m, 3H); 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) &#x3B4;
168.5, 153.0, 136.7, 133.2, 131.3, 129.8, 129.1, 127.5, 124.3, 124.1,
118.7.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, Ullmann coupling followed by Wittig reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Copper-catalyzed synthesis of benzo[b]thiophenes and benzothiazoles using
thiocarboxylic acids as a coupling partner
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Yu, Hui; Zhang, Meishu; Li, Yuzhe
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2013), 78(17), 8898-8903

