$DATUM (1S-exo)-2-Bornyl 2,4-Dinitrophenyl Sulfide (5): To a solution of 4 (1.00
g, 5.87 mmol) in EtOH (10 mL) is added one of NaOH (0.23 g, 5.75 mmol) in
EtOH (2 mL) and H2O (1 mL) followed by another of
2,4-dinitrochlorobenzene (1.17 g, 5.78 mmol) in EtOH (11 mL). The mixture
is stirred 10 min at 60 °C, then allowed to stand 18 h at 0°C. The yellow
crystalline product is isolated by suction and washed with cold EtOH; One
recystallization from heptane gives a analytical sample of 5. Yield 1.55
g, (80%). mp 144-146°C [α]D25 + 110.8° (c = 5.0, acetone). C16H20N2O4S
(336.4). calc. C 57.13 H 5.99 N 8.33 found 57.21 5.93 8.23. IR (KBr): ν =
1600 and 1500 (arom), 670 cm-1 (C-S). 1H-NMR (CDCl3/TMS): δ = 0.91, 1.07
and 1.10 (3s, 9H, 1-CH3 + C(CH3)2), 1.31-1.42 (m, 2H, H-5endo,6endo),
1.81-1.92 (m, 3 H, H-4,5exo,6exo), 2.05 (m, 1H, H-3exo), 2.14 (dd, 1H,
J3endo, 3exo = 12.2 Hz, J3endo, 2endo = - 8.7 Hz, H-3 endo), 3.41 (dd, 1
H, J2endo, 3endo = 8.7 Hz, J2endo, 3exo = 6.0 Hz, H-2 endo), 7.68 (d, 1
H, Jortho = 9.0 Hz, Harom-6), 8.34 (dd, 1 H, = 9.0 Hz, = 2.5 Hz,
Harom-5), 9.03 (d, 1 H, Jmeta = 2.5 Hz, Harom-3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of chiral sulfinic acids: sodium (1S-exo)-2-bornanesulfinate
