$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: From 1-Thioglycoses 2a, 2d-2g: To a
well-stirred suspension of K2CO3 (0.2 g) in acetone (20 mL) were added
sequentially 1-thioglycose (1 mmol), 4-nitrofluorobenzene (3b; 1.1 mmol)
and H2O (0.1 mL). The resulting mixture was stirred at r.t. for 0.3-4h
(Table), diluted with CH2Cl2 (20 mL), filtered and the solution was
evaporated. The expected compound was isolated by crystallization from
EtOH. 4g, yield 55%. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ = 1.98, 2.00, 2.02, 2.04, 2.06 (s.
21 H, CH3), 3.76 (m, 1 H, H-5), 3.95 (m, 2 H, H-4, H'-5), 4.05 (dd, J=
2.3, 12.4 Hz, 1H, H-6a), 4.21 (dd, J= 4.5, 12.4 Hz, 2 H, H-6a, H'-6b),
4.51 (dd, J= 2.6, 12.4 Hz, 1 H, H-6b), 4.82 (dd, J= 4.0, 7.5 Hz, 1 H,
H'-2), 4.83 (t, J= 9.0 Hz, 1 H, H-2), 4.84 (d, J= 9.0 Hz, 1 H, H-1), 5.01
(t, J= 10.0 Hz, 1 H, H'-4), 5.29 (m, 2H, H-3, H'-3), 5.36 (d, J= 4.0 Hz,
1H, H'-1), 7.51, 8.10 (m, 4Harom). mp (°C) found: 166; [α]D found (c,
CHCl3): - 40 (0.9); 13C NMR (CDCl3/TMS), δ (sugar ring carbons): 95.5
(C-1'), 83.7 (C-1), 76.2, 75.9, 72.3, 70.2, 69.8, 69.0, 68.5, 67.4, 62.6,
61.3
