$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (5-Bromo-2-nitrophenyl)(2-fluorophenyl)sulfane (18). Cesium carbonate
(4.3 g, 13.2 mmol) was added to a solution of 4-bromo-
2-fluoronitrobenzene 16 (2.42, 11 mmol, Aldrich) and 2-fluorobenzene
thiol 17 (1.4 g, 11 mmol, Aldrich) in DMF (60 mL), and the mixture was
stirred for 5 h at room temperature. Water (200 mL) and ethyl acetate
(100 mL) were added. The organic layer was separated and washed
sequentially with water (100 mL) and then brine (100 mL). The organic
phase was separated, dried, and concentrated to yield a yellow solid that
was purified by silica gel chromatography (hexanes/EtOAc 8:1 to 3:1). 18
(2.88 g, 80%). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 8.17 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H),
7.68-7.60 (m, 2H), 7.41-7.29 (m, 3H), 6.95 (s, 1H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
