$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of precursor molecule 34-58. General
procedure for the synthesis of precursor 34-49. To a stirred solution of
the corresponding thiophenol (1 eq) in anhydrous DMF (~3 mL per 1 mmol
thiol) K2CO3 (2 eq) was added, followed by the corresponding
para-haloginated-benzaldehyde or acetophenone (1 eq.). The reaction
mixture was then heated to 80°C until the reaction was completed. The
reaction mixture was allowed to cool to room temperature and partitioned
between 20 mL ether and 10 mL H2O. The phases were separated and the
aqueous layer was washed with ether (3 x 25 mL). The combined organic
layers were washed with 10 mL of H2O and 10 mL brine, dried over MgSO4
and concentrated in vacuo. The crude product was purified by silica gel
column chromatography using n-hexane/EtOAc mixtures or by
recrystallization from isopropyl alcohol to yield the pure product.
Reaction batch: 2-Methylbenzenethiol 61 (1.0 g, 8.1 mmol),
4-chloro-3-nitrobenzaldehyde (1.49 g, 8.1 mmol). Reaction batch:
2-Methylbenzenethiol 61 (62 mg, 0.5 mmol);
4-fluoro-3-(trifluoromethyl)benzaldehyde (96 mg, 0.5 mmol).
4-(o-Tolylthio)-3-(trifluoromethyl)benzaldehyde as a colorless oil, yield
124 mg, 0.4 mmol, 80%. TLC: (PE : EtOAc, 6:1): Rf = 0.5. 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 9.83 (s, 1H), 8.02 (d, J = 1.6 Hz, 1H), 7.61 (dd, J = 8.3, 1.4
Hz, 1H), 7.48 (dd, J = 7.6, 1.1 Hz, 1H), 7.36 - 7.31 (m, 1H), 7.31 - 7.27
(m, 1H), 7.24 - 7.17 (m, 1H), 6.76 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H), 2.24 (s, 3H). 13C
NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 190.05, 147.03, 143.21, 137.19, 132.92, 132.09,
131.69, 130.96, 128.75 (q, J = 1.6 Hz), 128.35 (q, J = 5.6 Hz), 127.99,
127.74, 127.54 (q, J = 31.9 Hz), 123.53 (q, J = 274.3 Hz), 20.66. 19F NMR
(376 MHz, CDCl3) δ -62.43. CHN analysis: C Hcalculated: C, 60.80; H,
3.74; found: C, 60.95; H, 4.07.
