$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4,5-Bis(2-ethylhexylthio)phthalonitrile (2): To a solution of
4,5-dichlorophthalonitrile (0.99 g, 5.0 mmol) in dimethylacetamide (15
mL) was added dry K2CO3 (2.0 g, 15.0 mmol). A stream of argon was passed
through the slurry for 10 minutes, after which 2-ethylhexanethiol was
added and the resulting mixture was heated at 90 °C for 8 h. It was then
poured into water and extracted with CH2Cl2. Solvents were evaporated in
vacuo to 2. Yellow oil, yield 1.7 g, 80%. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ
(ppm) = 0.85-0.93 (m, 12H, alkyl H), 1.26-1.31 (m, 8H, alkyl H),
1.40-1.54 (m, 8H, alkyl H), 1.64-1.72 (m, 2H, alkyl H), 2.91-2.99 (m, 4H,
CH2S), 7.4 (s, 2H, ArH). ESI-TOF MS: C24H36N2S2 m/z = 417.2 [M+H+].
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
