$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Phthalonitriles 3b,d,f,h;
4,5-Di(2,3,4,6-tetra-O-acetyl-1-thio-β-D-glucopyranosyl)phthalonitrile
(3b); Typical Procedure Bu4NOH (14 mL, 20 mmol) was added to a mixture of
4,5-difluorophthalonitrile (2b; 1.64 g, 10 mmol) and
2,3,4,6-tetra-O-acetyl-1-thio-β-D-glucopyranose (1b; 7.29 g, 20 mmol) in
CH2Cl2 (20 mL). The reaction mixture was stirred at r.t. for 48 h,
diluted with H2O (200 mL) and extracted with CH2Cl2 (2 × 100 mL). The
combined organic phases were washed with H2O (200 mL), dried (MgSO4), and
concentrated in vacuo. The obtained syrup purified by column
chromatography over silica gel using toluene-acetone (5:1).
4,5-Di(2,3,4,6-tetra-O-acetyl-1-thio-β-D-galactopyranosyl)phthalonitrile
(3d). Prepared from 2,3,4,6-tetra-O-acetyl-1-thio-β-D-galactopyranose
(1d, 1.46 g, 4 mmol) as described for compound 3b. Column chromatography
was carried out by using hexane-EtOAc (1:1) to afford 3d as a white
solid; yield: 1.36 g (80%). mp 108-112 °C; [α]D20 -18.8 (c 0.5, CHCl3).
1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.99 (s, 2 Harom), 5.46 (d, J4,3= 3.1 Hz, 2
H, H-4), 5.29 (t, J2,1 = J2,3 = 9.9 Hz, 2 H, H-2), 5.08 (dd, J3,2= 9.9
Hz, J3,4 = 3.1 Hz, 2 H, H-3), 4.78 (d, J1,2= 9.9 Hz, 2 H, H-1), 4.17-4.00
(m, 6 H, H-5, H-6a,b), 2.19, 2.08, 2.06, 1.96 (4 s, 4 × 6 H, CH3). 13C
NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 20.9, 21.0, 21.1, 21.4, 62.5, 66.6, 67.5, 71.9,
75.8, 84.5, 114.2, 115.5, 134.5, 142.8, 169.8, 170.2, 170.4, 170.9. HRMS
(FT-ICR): m/z [M + Na]+ calcd for C36H40N2O18S2 + Na: 875.1615; found:
875.16055. Anal. Calcd for C36H40N2O18S2: C, 50.70; H, 4.73; N, 3.28.
Found: C, 50.43; H, 4.47; N, 3.13.
