$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (2R,2'R,2''R,2'''R)-3,3',3'',3'''-[(5,8-Dihydroxy-1,4-dioxo-1,4-dihydronaphthalene-2,3,6,7-tetrayl)-tetrasulfanyl]tetrakis(2-acetylaminopropanoic
acid) (XIc). To 0.082 g (0.25 mmol) o f 2,3,6,7-tetrachloronaphthazarin
(Xc), 22 ml of CH3CN, and 12 ml of water was added at stirring 0.250 g
(1.53 mmol) of N-acetyl-L-cysteine and 0.256 g (2.0 mmol) of K2CO3. The
reaction progress was monitored by TLC in system C. After adding K2CO3
the reaction mixture turned violet. After 2 min the formation of four new
colored compounds was observed, Rf 0.68, 0.52, 0.40, and 0.22. After 2.5
h according to TLC the reaction mixture contained a single product of Rf
0.22. The reaction mixture was neutralized by adding the cationite
KU-2(H+), the resin was diltered off, the filtrate was evaporated in a
vacuum, from the residue by the preparative TLC in system C was isolated
of compound. Yield: 0.167 g, (80%); violet crystals. Rf 0.22 (C), mp
152-155°C. IR spectrum, cm-1: 3430(OH), 3380, 3353, 3323(NH), 3028, 1753,
1722(C═O), 1631(C═O), 1620, 1605(C═O), 1534(C═O), 1439, 1417, 1385, 1269,
1220, 1182, 1030, 829. 1H NMR spectrum (300 MHz), δ, ppm: 1.79 s (12H,
4COCH3), 3.39 d.d (4H, 4H1'A, J1'A,2' 8.8, J1'A,1'B 13.4 Hz), 3.64 d.d
(4H, 4H1'B, J1'B,2' 4.7, J1'B,1'A 13.4 Hz), 4.42 d.d.d (4H, 4H2', J2',1'A
8.8, J2',1'B 4.7, J2',NH 8.2 Hz), 8.28 d (4H, 4NH, JNH,2' 8.2 Hz), 12.88
br.s (4H, 4COOH), 13.33 s (2H, 2α-OH). 13C NMR spectrum (75 MHz), δ, ppm:
22.63, 35.88, 52.96, 110.68, 143.65, 169.62, 169.7, 171.9. High
resolution mass spectrum, m/z 857.0763 [M + Na]+. C30H34N4O16S4.
Calculated 857.0745.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
