$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of precursor molecule 34-58. General procedure for the
synthesis of precursor 34-49. To a stirred solution of the corresponding
thiophenol (1 eq) in anhydrous DMF (~3 mL per 1 mmol thiol) K2CO3 (2 eq)
was added, followed by the corresponding para-haloginated-benzaldehyde or
acetophenone (1 eq.). The reaction mixture was then heated to 80°C until
the reaction was completed. The reaction mixture was allowed to cool to
room temperature and partitioned between 20 mL ether and 10 mL H2O. The
phases were separated and the aqueous layer was washed with ether (3 x 25
mL). The combined organic layers were washed with 10 mL of H2O and 10 mL
brine, dried over MgSO4 and concentrated in vacuo. The crude product was
purified by silica gel column chromatography using n-hexane/EtOAc
mixtures or by recrystallization from isopropyl alcohol to yield the pure
product. Reaction batch: 2-Methylbenzenethiol 61 (1.0 g, 8.1 mmol),
4-chloro-3-nitrobenzaldehyde (1.49 g, 8.1 mmol).
3-Nitro-4-(o-tolylthio)benzaldehyde as a golden solid, yield 1.74 g, 6.4
mmol, 79%. M.p.: 91°C; TLC (PE : EtOAc, 4:1): Rf = 0.51. 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 9.97 (s, 1H), 8.73 (d, J = 1.7 Hz, 1H), 7.79 (dd, J = 8.5, 1.8
Hz, 1H), 7.59 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 7.48 (td, J = 7.5, 1.0 Hz, 1H), 7.43
(d, J = 7.0 Hz, 1H), 7.34 (td, J = 7.5, 0.9 Hz, 1H), 6.84 (d, J = 8.5 Hz,
1H), 2.36 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 189.17, 146.81, 144.95,
143.47, 137.23, 133.15, 132.09, 131.83, 131.53, 128.76, 128.22, 128.13,
128.10, 20.63. CHN analysis: calculated: C, 61.52; H, 4.06; N, 5.12;
found: C, 61.47; H, 4.01; N, 5.28.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
