$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Aryl Arenedithiocarboxylates 3; General
Procedure: To the stirred red solution of the sodium
arenedithiocarboxylate 1 (10 mmol) in t-BuOH (15mL) is slowly added the
appropriate iodonium salt 2 (10 mmol). The resultant mixture is stirred
at 70°C for the time given in the Table. The solvent is removed under
reduced pressure, H2O (15 mL) is added to the residue, and the resultant
mixture is extracted with CH2Cl2 (3x 10 mL). The extract is washed with
H2O (10 mL) and dried (MgSO4). The solvent is removed, hexane (10 mL) is
added to the residue, and the product is allowed to crystallize in a
refrigerator overnight. The crude product is isolated and recrystallized
from benzene/hexane. Product 3l, yield 79%. mp: 95-97 °C; Molecular
Formulab: C18H14S2 (294.3); 1H-NMR(CDCl3/TMS) δ : 2.42 (s, 3 H);
7.36-8.65 (m, 11 H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Polyvalent iodine in synthesis. 3. An efficient method for the synthesis
of aryl arenedithiocarboxylates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Chen, Zhen Chu; Jin, You Yuan; Yang, Rui Yang
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (1988), (9), 723-4

