$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2.2.4.4 bis [4-(p-aminothiophenyl)
benzoyl]diamine (ATPBA). Then 1 was converted to ATPBA 2 through
nucleophilic etherification: 1 reacted with 4-aminobenzenethiol in DMF at
155°C for 4 h as shown in Scheme 2. The reaction solution was then poured
into water. The resulting solid was filtered, washed with water and
methanol, then recrystallized from the mixture of water and DMF (1:1).
Bis[4-(p-aminothiophenyl)benzoyl] meta-phenylene diamine (2b), Yield:
78.6%, yellow sheet crystal. m.p.: 262-264°C, m/z (M-): 701.26. Chemical
shifts (═ ppm): H1 (5.617), H2 (6.651-6.672), H3 (7.084-7.105), H4
(7.203-7.224), H5 (7.809-7.830), H6 (7.895-7.917), H7 (7.973-7.995), H8
(10.514).
