$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
η6-2-Phenoxy-N,N-diethylbenzamide-η5-cyclopentadienyl Iron
Hexafluorophosphate (3a) and
η6-2-Thiophenoxy-N,N-diethylbenzamide-η5-cyclopentadienyl iron
hexafluorophosphate (3b): NaH (60% dispersion in mineral oil) (40 mg, 1.0
mmol) was placed in a two-necked flask under Ar and washed with 3 x 5 mL
of dry pentane. Dry THF (10 mL) was added, followed by 0.82 mmol of
phenol or thiophenol. After stirring at r.t. for 30 min, 2 (300 mg, 0.62
mmol) was added, and the mixture was stirred at r.t. for 3 h. The
solution was then diluted with 40 mL of CH2Cl2 and washed with 3 x 20 mL
of water containing approximately 1 g of NH4PF6 per portion. Drying over
Na2SO4, filtration and evaporation afforded crude material which was
purified by recrystallization from acetone-diethylether. Compound 3b as
yellow-brown crystals, yield 275 mg, 79%. IR (KBr): 1634 and 1287 cm-1.
HRMS-FAB+ (m/z): M+ calcd for C22H24FeNOS 406.0928; found 406.0938. 1H
NMR (CD3COCD3): δ 1.12 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 3H), 1.29 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 3H),
3.17-3.28 (m, 1H), 3.29-3.38 (m, 1H), 3.41-3.50 (m, 1H), 3.75-3.86 (m,
1H), 5.29 (s, 5H), 6.13-6.16 (m, 1H), 6.44-6.47 (m, 2H), 6.73-6.77 (m,
1H), 7.60-7.64 (m, 3H), 7.75-7.79 (m, 2H). 13C NMR (CD3COCD3): δ 13.4,
14.7, 41.3, 44.5, 81.3 (Cp), 85.6, 86.1, 87.2, 88.9, 105.5, 109.0, 130.0,
132.0, 132.1, 136.7, 164.0.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
